>walk to the sandwich hut

The Sandwich Hut
A low hut with a wide shutter that folds down into a counter. This is where your
life happens. Shelves and a cool pit hold the ingredients, a chopping board sits
in the middle of the counter, and the knife hangs from its nail. The village
green is back to the west.

On the counter are a loaf of bread and a sandwich knife. In the cool pit are
some pickled roots. On the pantry shelf are some honey and some herb curd.

Hob leans on the counter with the air of a man who has been waiting since before
the sun. 

>talk to hob
You could ASK Hob ABOUT something (his lunch, say). Or just type your question.

>what does hob want?
(Asking Hob.)
"Same as always," says Hob. "Meat and sourberry, thick as you like. And no
pickle. I have views about pickle."

>where is the meat?
You haven't the faintest idea, and nobody here looks any better informed. You
can EXAMINE things, ASK people about them, or type /HINT for a nudge.

>who is dunna?
You haven't the faintest idea, and nobody here looks any better informed. You
can EXAMINE things, ASK people about them, or type /HINT for a nudge.

>i want to make a sandwich with meat and berries
There is no cured meat in the cool pit at the moment. Dunna smokes the
village's, and she is not handing it over yet.

>go east
