>go to the orchard please

The Orchard Slope
A gentle slope of sourberry bushes, planted by someone with ambition and tended
by someone with a scarf. The bushes are low and thorny and heavy with small
purple berries; bees move among them like a committee. The village is back to
the north.

Sourberries cling to the bushes in thorny profusion. 

>could you take the berries
You pick a handful and immediately have nowhere to put them. A basket would
help.

>climb the bushes
Climbing that would achieve little.

>what is a babel fish?
The Babel fish: a small yellow thing that lives in your ear, feeds on the
brainwaves of whoever is near, and in return translates every language you hear
into your own. It is such a useful coincidence that some people take it as proof
of something. You have never had the energy to find out what. There is one in a
jar in your hut.

>tell hob about the weather
You can't see anything like that here. (LOOK and INVENTORY will remind you what
is around.)

