>go to the smokehouse

The Smokehouse
A squat hut of black timber, whose single room is a perpetual early evening.
Racks of curing meat hang in the smoke. A chopping block stands by the door with
a cleaver on it. The smoke finds your eyes in about a second and a half. A path
leads back northwest to the village green.

Dunna stands at the racks, watching the meat as though it might try something. 

>ask dunna about her cleaver
"Blunt as a tax," says Dunna. "It wants a good stone. The river has one, if you
can find it. Under something heavy, I'd have said."

>take cleaver
It is Dunna's, and she is standing right there.

>examine smoke
Dark sides of meat, curing in a smoke so thick you could set a spoon in it.

